   "found": [],
   "note": "NEGATIVE, recorded so the candidate is not re-offered. Leaf 5 is an ADVERTISER page -- printed p.5 under the running head 'BROOKLYN DIRECTORY ADVERTISER', a Barstow Elevated Oven Range engraving for G. G. Hallett, printed on YELLOW stock. Phase 0b's title for this row is from the same section ('BROOKLYN DIRECTORY ADVERTISER. CLARK'S BRYANT & STRATTON Brooklyn Business College'), i.e. an ad misread as the title page -- the 1856BPL failure again. The row's year, publisher and legend are all correct, so only `title` is wrong. GENERALISABLE: 'BROOKLYN DIRECTORY ADVERTISER' is a RUNNING HEAD, and running heads are the cheapest possible ad-run detector for the phase-2 ad inventory -- no layout analysis needed, just a regex over the top line. Several BPL volumes carry it (1856, 1871, micro_IABROOKLYN_0038), and the tinted paper is a second, independent signal."
  },
